-- title:
--   Vélu's maps for an odd-order point in reduced rational form
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with decidable equality, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $F$, $n$ a natural number, and $Q$ a point of the associated affine curve whose additive order is exactly $2n+1$. Form the finite set $\Sigma \subseteq F\times F$ of coordinate pairs of the multiples $k\cdot Q$ for $1\le k\le n$ (the point at infinity contributing $(0,0)$). The assertion is that there exist polynomials $P, S, N_0, N_1, R \in F[x]$ and a finite set $B \subseteq F$ such that: $P$ is monic; $\deg P = \deg S + 1$; $P$ and $S$ are coprime; for every $x,y \in F$ with $(x,y)$ a nonsingular point of the affine curve, $x \in B$ if and only if the corresponding point lies in the subgroup generated by $Q$; and for every $x \notin B$ one has $S(x)\neq 0$, $R(x)\neq 0$, $$x + \sum_{(x_0,y_0)\in\Sigma}\Bigl(\frac{t}{x-x_0} + \frac{u}{(x-x_0)^2}\Bigr) = \frac{P(x)}{S(x)},$$ and, for every $y \in F$, $$y - \sum_{(x_0,y_0)\in\Sigma}\Bigl(\frac{u\,(2y+a_1x+a_3)}{(x-x_0)^3} + \frac{t\,(a_1(x-x_0)+y-y_0)}{(x-x_0)^2} + \frac{a_1u - g_xg_y}{(x-x_0)^2}\Bigr) = \frac{N_0(x)+N_1(x)\,y}{R(x)},$$ where $g_x = 3x_0^2+2a_2x_0+a_4-a_1y_0$, $g_y = -(2y_0+a_1x_0+a_3)$, $t = 2g_x - a_1g_y$ and $u = g_y^2$.
--
--   This puts Vélu's explicit formulae for the quotient of $W$ by the cyclic group generated by a point of odd order into the standard separable shape $(x,y)\mapsto\bigl(P(x)/S(x),\,(N_0(x)+N_1(x)y)/R(x)\bigr)$ with $P$ monic, $\deg P = \deg S + 1$ and $\gcd(P,S)=1$, valid away from the abscissae of the nonzero points of the kernel. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.veluPointHom_mem_rationalHomSet_and_exists_mem_rationalHomSet_comp_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.veluPointHom_mem_rationalHomSet_and_exists_mem_rationalHomSet_comp_eq) to exhibit Vélu's homomorphism as given by rational functions over $F$ and to feed it into the factorisation of an isogeny through a separable one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_veluX_eq_div_and_veluY_eq_div_of_addOrderOf_eq.lean

